cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "CoverWeave: a loss-tolerant distributed algorithm for minimum-weight connected capacitated vertex cover in wireless sensor networks"
abstract: >-
  CoverWeave is a distributed protocol that builds a connected, capacitated
  vertex cover for link monitoring in wireless sensor networks from one-hop
  rules over a backbone, and keeps working when radio messages are lost. The
  repository holds the protocol, an independent validator, three execution
  backends and the pre-registered evaluation of the manuscript.
